==Economy==
{{Main|Economy of Hesperia}}

{{See also|Economy of Balisca}}
[[File:Città Antica and station, Alessandria.png|left|thumb|340x340px|[[Alessandria]], the economic capital of Hesperia, is one of the most prominent {{W|financial center}}s in the {{W|Western Hemisphere}}.]]
Hesperia maintains an {{W|advanced economy|advanced}} {{W|socialist market economy}}, which ranks amongst the largest in Latin America. If Hesperia was an independent nation, its economy would ranking as the fourth-largest in Latin America and the thirty-second largest in the world. Historically being a driver of [[Balisca#Economic history and growth|Balisca's industrialization]] and the primary gateway for immigrants, it has since entered a period of sustained {{W|economic degrowth}} since the 1990s. Nevertheless, it remains a highly industrialized economy, with one of Latin America's highest quality of life as of 2025 and the ?th-highest {{W|Human Development Index}}. The community is well known for its creative and innovative cooperatives, an efficient and competitive agricultural sector (with Abyala's second-largest wine production), and for its influential and high-quality automobile, shipbuilding, machinery, food, design and [[W:Fashion industry|fashion]] industries.

